+    # 1-chunk ones (decode rows riding along as 1-token extends). The CUDA scan
+    # is ~2.5x faster per chunk step on the long sequences but slower on the
+    # 1-chunk CTAs (one resident CTA per SM), so take it while the long CTAs
+    # fit in one wave and the serial-scan saving (~1.1 us per chunk of the
+    # longest sequence) outweighs the short-CTA cost (~1.2 us per 1-chunk
+    # sequence), both measured on B200. Reuses prepare_chunk_indices' host
+    # list, so no extra device->host read.
+    counts = prepare_chunk_counts(cu_seqlens, CHUNK_SIZE)
+    n_long = sum(1 for c in counts if c > 1)
+    return ctas_per_seq * n_long <= num_sms and 11 * max(counts) > 12 * (N - n_long)
